"""
Figure 4: HILIC loading optimization (Phase 2) — CORRECTED, transparent background.

Single-tip GF-C tandem IMAC-HILIC at 4 HILIC resin loadings (10 / 5 / 2 / 1 mg).
Self-contained. 8 panels in 2x4 layout.

CORRECTIONS vs. the earlier version:
  1. GP intensity columns selected with str.startswith(prefix), NOT `prefix in col`.
     `'10_10_GP' in col` also matched the FragPipe decoy columns
     'REV10_10_GP_*', inflating the 10 mg condition with reverse (false) hits.
     startswith() excludes them. Only the 10 mg condition was affected because
     its prefix is a substring of the REV-prefixed decoy column names.
  2. GP intensity columns exclude MaxLFQ columns (`'MaxLFQ' not in col`).
     Including them double-counts each peptide (one raw + one MaxLFQ column),
     inflating per-replicate detection.
  3. GP-fraction composition (Panel B) uses the deduction method:
       - N-glycopeptides : has_glyco
       - Phosphopeptides : has_phospho AND NOT has_glyco
       - Other           : everything else (Total - N-glyco - phospho)
     'Other' absorbs both truly unmodified peptides and peptides bearing only
     other modifications (e.g. oxidation). The three categories sum to 100%.
     Counting is at the deduplicated (Peptide Sequence + glycan mass) level.

Output background is transparent (RGBA) for overlay on slides / posters.

Data:
    1150375-1150394_HILIC_beads-PP_A227_20260410_Peptide_Precursor_Report.csv  (PP fraction, Spectronaut)
    1150410-1150429_HILIC_beads_test_GP_A227_combined_modified_peptide.tsv     (GP fraction, FragPipe)

Panels (2x4):
    A: N-glycopeptide count bar
    B: GP fraction composition (N-glyco / Phos / Other) %
    C: Glyco CV grouped bar (Total / CV<20% / CV<10%)
    D: Glycan classification stacked %  (5-class incl. Hybrid)
    E: Saccharide count violin
    F: Phosphopeptide count stacked (mono / multi)
    G: PP fraction selectivity stacked %
    H: Phosphopeptide CV violin
"""
